From f87f3640d4abcfbcfe54c3f69ec30bbf44aac39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:46:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] tutorial: end it once a gamepad is playing

Hypothesis: the tutorial's popups name the keyboard and the mouse, and turning with a stick goes through
`pad_look`, which never tells the tutorial. So on a handheld "Look around" never closes, and the
"Move with W, A, S and D" and "Use your mouse to turn" hints stay on screen for good.

Change: once the pad has driven the game, the tutorial ends the way its last step does, and that's
persisted the way each of its steps is. So `tutorialStep` in options.txt becomes none, like any player
who finished it. A player on keyboard and mouse keeps the tutorial.

Number: popups on screen after moving with a pad: before, always (seen on the R36S). After, none.

Falsified by: a tutorial popup on screen after the pad has been used.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/horizon-client/src/game/tutorial.rs | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/horizon-client/src/game/tutorial.rs b/crates/horizon-client/src/game/tutorial.rs
index bb77cda..0e01a48 100644
--- a/crates/horizon-client/src/game/tutorial.rs
+++ b/crates/horizon-client/src/game/tutorial.rs
@@ -82,6 +82,11 @@ impl Tutorial {
         true
     }
 
+    /// The tutorial is over, as when its last step ends. Returns whether the persisted step changed.
+    pub(super) fn finish(&mut self) -> bool {
+        self.set_step(Step::None)
+    }
+
     pub(super) fn input(&mut self) {
         self.moved = true;
     }
@@ -257,6 +262,14 @@ impl super::Game<'_> {
         {
             return;
         }
+        // Its hints name the keyboard and the mouse, and a stick's turning doesn't count as looking
+        // around, so with a pad its first step could never end.
+        if self.pad.in_use {
+            if self.tutorial.finish() {
+                self.persist_tutorial_step();
+            }
+            return;
+        }
         if self.screen == super::Screen::Playing
             && ([
                 KeyCode::KeyW,
